    "recommendations": "Reducing fuel continuity within the immediate structure perimeter should be a primary focus, as dense and continuous shrub cover surrounding the residence could limit defensible space and reduce opportunities for suppression operations near the structure. Thinning and separating shrub masses closest to the building, and creating meaningful gaps within the heavier brush concentrations, may reduce the ability of surface fire to travel uninterrupted toward the structure. Managing vegetation along the length of the driveway would support firefighter access and improve evacuation conditions, particularly given the extended travel distance involved. Maintaining cleared margins on both sides of the access route and reducing overhanging or encroaching vegetation could improve visibility and passability during an incident. Preserving and expanding any existing open terrain around the property could serve as a natural fuel break, and continuing to manage vegetation concentrations adjacent to the structure over time would support long-term wildfire resilience and property preparedness."
